  "topicId": "puc1-physics-11-thermodynamics.t1",
  "stem": {
   "en": "One mole of an ideal gas is heated at constant pressure from 300 K to 400 K. The work done by it is about (R = 8.31 J mol⁻¹ K⁻¹):"
